// Read/write one grid cell. grid_set uses the generic lset "store into an
// imported list" idiom (see demos/gl3dgame/world/game/state/mutate.id):
// passing the imported list as a parameter makes it an assignable identifier
// again, and lists are reference-semantic so the store is shared.

grid_get(int column, int row) {
  int cell_value = (import maze_grid)[row * (import grid_width) + column];
} return int cell_value;
given create_maze (0, 0):(1)
given create_maze (14, 12):(1)
given open_room_setup (1, 1):(0)

grid_set(int column, int row, int new_cell_value) {
  int flat_index = row * (import grid_width) + column;
  integer_list_set((import maze_grid), flat_index, new_cell_value);
} return void;
given create_maze (3, 4, 0):() then grid_sample_cell:(0)
given create_maze (3, 4, 7):() then grid_sample_cell:(7)

// Test check: cell (3,4) read through a zero-argument wrapper, since a
// `then` check takes none but grid_get needs both coordinates.
grid_sample_cell() {
  int sample_value = grid_get(3, 4);
} return int sample_value;
given create_maze ():(1)
given create_maze ():(1) then calls grid_get:(3, 4)
